sByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://i.pinimg.com/564x/13/c3/2d/13c32d0e6c278e6809ae098477df40a7.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T08:27:19-07:00","id":1209264,"title":"","content":"First, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1757_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1757\" data-vbnamecard=\"1757\">Acrozatarim</a> have we told you today how blessed the community is to have you engaged here, with such prodigious ideation at work? You inspire, and someday when I grow up I hope to contribute even one thing of worth aspiring to yours!<br /> <br /> This is really fantastic: a sketch of core ideas and just enough of a framework to build on. Well. More than that, as you give stats and everything! (Which is a real heavy lift, as you know.)<br /> <br /> How do you think these &quot;frost giants&quot; might interact with the other giant legends? Especially of the British Isles and Ireland, where giants were regarded as precursors and contemporaries at least up until the Britons were hammered into the edges at the end of the 6th Century. I'm thinking of Fomorians of course, and also &quot;good&quot; giants like Bran the Blessed--ones that in CofD could be linked to the Hedge and Arcadia. That... wouldn't stop Ymir, frankly; he comes across as a cross-splat antagonist even if he (it?) primarily cares about Fenris.<br /> <br /> Why do you think Hel turned on the Urathra? Something drove her out and twisted her outlook badly, for her to side with Ymir. Any ideas?<br /> <br /> What would you make Angrboda and is she then the mother of Hel? Angrboda is also the mother of Fenrir, which is obviously an error, but she's mixed up heavily in these legends and it seems a shame to leave her out of this apocalyptic rewriting/mythic start! (And if she dwells in the Iron Wood, I'd place that in Finland or northern Russia....)<br /> <br /> How do you think other splats would react to this set of events--first in the background and then effectively bending Scandinavian culture into going a-viking with a red fury as only the Darkness can induce.<br /> <br /> Very cool.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a> I think for hive-claimed the answer is &quot;they look like all of those pics&quot;--how the appearance of what was once human(-ish) twists is going to be very dependent on which spirits of what power are contained in him. In fact, appearance clues may be all the wolves get to start puzzling out how to deal with it, as a hive-claimed can be one of the most dangerous individual challenges shy of idigam. (Or, a well-developed fellow werewolf.)<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12493,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","user":"Khanwulf","date":".  Angrboda.... 04-20-2018, 11:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-19T09:37:20-07:00","id":1220266,"title":"","content":"I think that Jotnar could easily look like Ancients from the new <b>God of War</b> ( Subtitled 'Kratos Norse Adeventures' <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) - see below<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6F8l7wPxvWw\" data-code=\"6F8l7wPxvWw\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/6F8l7wPxvWw/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-19T09:59:06-07:00","id":1220269,"title":"","content":"I'm not Chris Allen, but I did some my own a bit research of Norse myths for the CoD games in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1047550-dark-eras-wolf-and-raven-nine-realms\"><b>Nine Realms</b> topic</a>. To be frank, it's idea start was inspired by Chris own stuff posted here. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> So I share my takes on them, as Chris is not answering for now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1031595-dark-eras-the-fall-of-fenris?p=1209264#post1209264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you think these &quot;frost giants&quot; might interact with the other giant legends? Especially of the British Isles and Ireland, where giants were regarded as precursors and contemporaries at least up until the Britons were hammered into the edges at the end of the 6th Century. I'm thinking of Fomorians of course, and also &quot;good&quot; giants like Bran the Blessed--ones that in CofD could be linked to the Hedge and Arcadia. That... wouldn't stop Ymir, frankly; he comes across as a cross-splat antagonist even if he (it?) primarily cares about Fenris.</div> </div> </div> </div>If we go outside of <b>Werewolf</b> gameline, most often I would connect various Giants races with <b>Beast</b>'s Anakim. Like in Norse myths, many times those Giants are said to be able to look like normal human - and then becoming enormous in next second. Just like Anakim can. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Of course, using <b>Changeling</b> and, for example, Hobgoblins is totally doable also. But still, I would more stick with Anakims only because that Beasts are much more connected to the Material / Flesh World in the first place, as their Horrors strife from <b>humans fears </b>- Jotunheim is described in Norse myths to look more or less as Flesh World.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1031595-dark-eras-the-fall-of-fenris?p=1209264#post1209264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why do you think Hel turned on the Urathra? Something drove her out and twisted her outlook badly, for her to side with Ymir. Any ideas?</div> </div> </div> </div>I literally use Hel as nickname of local Bale Hounds cult leader in my modern Sweden game ( that also thinks is real goddess Hel ). I would generally simply point Hel in cosmology as local manifestation of whatever Maeljins really are. Or that Hel is person for Soulless Wolf, see below.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1031595-dark-eras-the-fall-of-fenris?p=1209264#post1209264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would you make Angrboda and is she then the mother of Hel? Angrboda is also the mother of Fenrir, which is obviously an error, but she's mixed up heavily in these legends and it seems a shame to leave her out of this apocalyptic rewriting/mythic start! (And if she dwells in the Iron Wood, I'd place that in Finland or northern Russia....)</div> </div> </div> </div>Years before Chris write-up opening topic I remade 'classical', American myth about creation of Uratha from relation of Father Wolf and Mother Luna into Norse version of it - in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1046705-dark-eras-mother-wolf-for-norse-uratha\">where Wolf Mother made love with Father Mani ( Moon God in Norse myths )</a>. Lack of love and compassion from gods later on finally made Wolf Mother into Angerboda, that literally means 'One Who Brings Grief'. It exactly made Fenris as one of Firstborn, but also J\u00f6rmungandras cousin to werewolves, but it's only one small problem for Uratha historians saying 'human get it wrong'. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> In reality, I much more equating Wolf Mother with being <i>literal</i> Dark Mother of Begotten Beasts - this way she easily can be both parent to the Fenrir, J\u00f6rmungandr, Hel and all other - Wolf Mother was just her Wolf persona in Pangea. And that Wolf is dead it can imply that Dark Mother in Primordial Dream is all the Astral memory of this Mother being. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> And that Hel can be <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/360414-souless-wolf-as-urfarah-remains\">Soulless Wolf that is sometimes implied to come to being AFTER death of Mother Wolf</a>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1031595-dark-eras-the-fall-of-fenris?p=1209264#post1209264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you think other splats would react to this set of events--first in the background and then effectively bending Scandinavian culture into going a-viking with a red fury as only the Darkness can induce.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do not understand this question - Could you rephrase it? Or maybe adding more exmples in what you have in mind?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-19-2018, 01:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T08:37:40-07:00","id":1220848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1031595-dark-eras-the-fall-of-fenris?p=1220269#post1220269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I literally use Hel as nickname of local Bale Hounds cult leader in my modern Sweden game ( that also thinks is real goddess Hel ). I would generally simply point Hel in cosmology as local manifestation of whatever Maeljins really are. Or that Hel is person for Soulless Wolf, see below.</div> </div> </div> </div>For this particular material we have written (by Chris) that Hel is a bale wolf of great and sorcerous power. I'm just fishing for how that might have come about... even bad guys have origins, regardless of how lost they might be. In this case, we have defined that Hel is: female, known to the Uratha, then either became Bale and was expelled for her horrible crimes, or committed horrible crimes and was driven away where she found the Maeljin.<br /> <br /> Which of these seems likely and what might she have done that horrified the Uratha so? I'm just presuming that being &quot;Bale&quot; is not enough to truly horrify.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1031595-dark-eras-the-fall-of-fenris?p=1220269#post1220269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Years before Chris write-up opening topic I remade 'classical', American myth about creation of Uratha from relation of Father Wolf and Mother Luna into Norse version of it - in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1046705-dark-eras-mother-wolf-for-norse-uratha\">where Wolf Mother made love with Father Mani ( Moon God in Norse myths )</a>. Lack of love and compassion from gods later on finally made Wolf Mother into Angerboda, that literally means 'One Who Brings Grief'. It exactly made Fenris as one of Firstborn, but also J\u00f6rmungandras cousin to werewolves, but it's only one small problem for Uratha historians saying 'human get it wrong'. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> In reality, I much more equating Wolf Mother with being <i>literal</i> Dark Mother of Begotten Beasts - this way she easily can be both parent to the Fenrir, J\u00f6rmungandr, Hel and all other - Wolf Mother was just her Wolf persona in Pangea. And that Wolf is dead it can imply that Dark Mother in Primordial Dream is all the Astral memory of this Mother being. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> And that Hel can be <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/360414-souless-wolf-as-urfarah-remains\">Soulless Wolf that is sometimes implied to come to being AFTER death of Mother Wolf</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea that the Dark Mother is an astral memory of Urfarah is an interesting tie. My knowledge of Beast is extremely thin--thinner than Mage, which is definitely &quot;butter over too much bread&quot;. Werewolf isn't much better, which is why I pick at questions.<br /> <br /> Anyway, my inclination is to try and make Angrboda into a real person, with whom PCs might interact, and then use some of the back-story beats of Chris' arc to set things up. That means trying to understand the players and their relationships better. I could handwave Angrboda away as just incorporated into the legend, but since we know human legends are going to be a warped reflection anyway it seems like a waste to not use her.<br /> <br /> So basically a timeline, with speculation:<br /> <br /> 1. In the distant past, Ymir is born of a hive-claiming and is oppressed by Fenrir, who earns its enduring enmity. Alternatively, a great and cunningly malevolent spirit escapes (at least in part) from Fenrir, and flees to a forbidding land where it &quot;goes native&quot; by creating a hive-claimed with powerful allies it recruits--ancient spirits that remember Urfarah, and hate him and his children nearly as much as the spirit hates Fenrir. [For the sake of linking, let's say the side-effects of this claiming, or perhaps a very early attempt to eliminate Ymir (by Fenrir?), resulted in the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Storegga_Slide\" target=\"_blank\">Storegga Slide</a>.]<br /> <br /> 2. By the time of Rome's height (which means, not later than 2nd century AD) Ymir has embedded himself, hidden, in the far North.<br /> <br /> 2. Angrboda (who might also be a hive-claimed giantess, or she achieves this reputation later) begets Hel from Loki in the forest to the east of the Baltic. Hel is wolf-blooded and suffers the Change, joining the Uratha but either falling prey to the Maeljin or carrying with her the seeds of their influence from an early age. She is driven out, to Utgard (the forest, outside) and wanders.<br /> <br /> 3. Hel encounters Ymir, or is introduced to him.<br /> <br /> 4. Fenrir is drawn in and imprisoned. The Blood Talons start going mad, first with attempts to figure out what's happening, then to save him, and to gather resources for such. [&quot;Viking&quot; settlement movement? Which pre-dates the raids.]<br /> <br /> 5. Circa 793, the Blood Talon seers proclaim that imitation of Fenrir will strengthen him and enable his freedom. The Viking Age is launched. Blood Talons spur the human kingdoms to greed and war that quickly turns into more convenient measures such as settlement to facilitate the process, and then more settlement. The response from Europe includes redoubled efforts to Christianize the North, and by the 11th and 12th centuries going a-viking is essentially done, [which implies that Fenrir was freed?]<br /> <br /> Since I'm working forward from the 5th century with my own players, penciling in more will be helpful.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1031595-dark-eras-the-fall-of-fenris?p=1220269#post1220269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do not understand this question - Could you rephrase it? Or maybe adding more exmples in what you have in mind?</div> </div> </div> </div>My question was &quot;how does this plot and background for viking raids affect other splats?&quot; I mean, Mages might notice something was wrong, first. Vampires care only about their resource base (people). Changelings would interpret things differently, and look for an Other reason for the feared Vikings. And etc. What could draw them back toward the real problem, which is Fenrir and more or less the end of the world, from the Uratha/Blood Talon perspective?<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf<br /> <br /> PS. And thanks for the response, Wyrd.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12493,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","user":"Khanwulf","date":".  Fixed formatting 05-21-2018, 05:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T08:47:27-07:00","id":1220851,"title":"","content":"Now, I could be misremembering things, but I believe in the era in question, the majority of mages during the period in the area were a group that would come to be called liches and reapers in the modern era. They are mages who harvest souls to empower themselves and extend their lifespans (at least that\u2019s the general impression others have). There would no doubt be some will workers who aren\u2019t affiliated with them about, but they probably keep their heads down/only work on a local level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T08:57:27-07:00","id":1220855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gullinbursti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1031595-dark-eras-the-fall-of-fenris?p=1220851#post1220851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, I could be misremembering things, but I believe in the era in question, the majority of mages during the period in the area were a group that would come to be called liches and reapers in the modern era. They are mages who harvest souls to empower themselves and extend their lifespans (at least that\u2019s the general impression others have). There would no doubt be some will workers who aren\u2019t affiliated with them about, but they probably keep their heads down/only work on a local level.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not a majority, but they were an equal order in the Diamond (and the other orders didn't know about them being liches and reapers).<br /> <br /> <b>Edit:</b> Diamond, not Pentacle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":4433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","user":"Second Chances","date":". 05-21-2018, 02:54 PM"