Roman Empire</a> - and spread with it - I would suspect that Norse Awakened has no Orders - only the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/589983-dark-eras-great-cults-of-major-religions\">Norse mages Great Cult is in the North</a>. And there is large part of them as <i>Seo Hel</i>, Nordic witches dedicated to Hel that were among the most feared mages in the North. They believed their patron represented the spiritual reflection of physical decay and that the material and physical realms retain a bond with the soul upon death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-21-2018, 02:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T11:53:38-07:00","id":1220894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1031595-dark-eras-the-fall-of-fenris?p=1220888#post1220888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/387074-history-of-awakened-mage-timeline#post387074&amp;quot;]As</a> Diamond Orders were (probably) created in Roman Empire[/URL] - and spread with it - I would suspect that Norse Awakened has no Orders - only the <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/589983-dark-eras-great-cults-of-major-religions&amp;quot;]Norse</a> Mages' Great Cult is in the North[/URL]. And there is large part of them as <i>Seo Hel</i>, Nordic witches dedicated to Hel that were among the most feared mages in the North. They believed their patron represented the spiritual reflection of physical decay and that the material and physical realms retain a bond with the soul upon death.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Orders didn't spread with the Roman Empire though, they were explicitly a worldwide phenomenon. They were in North America before the settlers came and they were in Africa before the colonists arrived. There probably were Nameless Orders like you describe amongst the Norse, but the Diamond assuredly existed there too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T12:17:12-07:00","id":1220900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1031595-dark-eras-the-fall-of-fenris?p=1220894#post1220894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Orders didn't spread with the Roman Empire though, they were explicitly a worldwide phenomenon. They were in North America before the settlers came and they were in Africa before the colonists arrived. There probably were Nameless Orders like you describe amongst the Norse, but the Diamond assuredly existed there too.</div> </div> </div> </div>But HOW? Norse people are once German tribes from Europe that moved on North in circa 1st century AD - and more or less lost contact with main continent up to start of Viking Age in circa 793 AD. I can easily see that once Vikings get in contact with ex-Roman Empire kingdoms and Orders in them - Silver Ladders 'missionaries' go to North and join Norse culture, spreading Diamond Orders there. And from there, now Norse Orders joined expedition of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Erik_the_Red\" target=\"_blank\">Erik the Red</a>, spreading their influence to now modern Canada and from there into Native American people in Americas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-21-2018, 04:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T12:43:52-07:00","id":1220908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1031595-dark-eras-the-fall-of-fenris?p=1220900#post1220900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But HOW?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Mages are known to have a few travel and communication expediting means available to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T13:24:00-07:00","id":1220922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1031595-dark-eras-the-fall-of-fenris?p=1220900#post1220900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But HOW? .</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to be flippant... but by magic. Teleportation with Space and telepathic links via Mind are the two most obvious ones, but the greatest trick Mages have in their favour is likely the exact same one that made the Wise so successful in The Sundered World: the Astral.<br /> <br /> Mage from very different regions can gather in the Temenos to convene and trade notes. They can also use the Astral to spy on different cultures (and Mages) then steal the good bits. Studying people from across the world would make for a good obsession for a Mage. Give it enough time and the evolutions of various groups will start to converge into similar forms, so when they meet, they acknowledge each other as being part of the same Order, even if their hierarchies don't overlap.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T13:44:28-07:00","id":1220929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1031595-dark-eras-the-fall-of-fenris?p=1220922#post1220922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to be flippant... but by magic. Teleportation with Space and telepathic links via Mind</div> </div> </div> </div>To use Space Teleporation you must have Sympathy - i.e. 'know' the place in the first place. The Norse, for the Europeans in 9th century, were totally alien people by the 8 centuries of separation from their Germanic forefathers. I would suspect this does not count as Sympathy on any real matter to be used. Same can goes with Mind that without Space component is limited only to what you see - and Germanic mages did not see Norse one in the long time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1031595-dark-eras-the-fall-of-fenris?p=1220922#post1220922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mage from very different regions can gather in the Temenos to convene and trade notes. They can also use the Astral to spy on different cultures (and Mages) then steal the good bits. Studying people from across the world would make for a good obsession for a Mage. Give it enough time and the evolutions of various groups will start to converge into similar forms, so when they meet, they acknowledge each other as being part of the same Order, even if their hierarchies don't overlap.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would point that Norse culture was a large shock to the early Medival Christandom, it was so alien to them. So this mean that Astral Realms of German and protoNorse would be more and more separated, ending in probably 2nd century AD as 'alien' Realms - so not related, i.e. not connected in Astral. When Germans become Christians, similar Astral Realms become almost non-existing, ending with separated Christian-Germans realms and Norseman realms, not having any more connection.<br /> <br /> <b>I can see Orders slowly conquering any land they are neighbor - but they need to have <i>whatever long contact</i> for that to work.</b> That's why Orders can be on Silk Road in the same time ( circa 2nd to 9th century ) - because Eastern Roman Empire have contacts with Turks, those with India ( that had already proto-Orders as Darshanas ) and China is just around corner. <b>HOWEVER protoNorse literally cut off their contacts with the old continent on migration, passing what would be described as Small Ice Age on the North.</b> So I do not see any Awakened contacts between Orders ( that did not converted Germans in 1st century AD ) and local Great Cults of Norse mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-21-2018, 04:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T14:12:01-07:00","id":1220936,"title":"","content":"That is literally not how any of this works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T14:19:14-07:00","id":1220938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1031595-dark-eras-the-fall-of-fenris?p=1220929#post1220929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To use Space Teleporation you must have Sympathy - i.e. 'know' the place in the first place. The Norse, for the Europeans in 9th century, were totally alien people by the 8 centuries of separation from their Germanic forefathers. I would suspect this does not count as Sympathy on any real matter to be used. Same can goes with Mind that without Space component is limited only to what you see - and Germanic mages did not see Norse one in the long time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Space lets you move faster by compressing distances, Forces lets you fly. Spirit lets you take shortcuts through the Shadow and enlist Spirits for aid.<br /> <br /> Seriously - if a Mage wants to go exploring, there are few things to stop them. Whenever the Sleepers catch up is meaningless.<br /> <br /> (I mean, I'm working on a Proximus Dynasty that are basically some flavor of ninja, and they have a branch in Scotland due to ancient Portal/Iris hijinks. Pretty much just so I can have McNinjas)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1031595-dark-eras-the-fall-of-fenris?p=1220929#post1220929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would point that Norse culture was a large shock to the early Medival Christandom, it was so alien to them. So this mean that Astral Realms of German and protoNorse would be more and more separated, ending in probably 2nd century AD as 'alien' Realms - so not related, i.e. not connected in Astral. When Germans become Christians, similar Astral Realms become almost non-existing, ending with separated Christian-Germans realms and Norseman realms, not having any more connection.<br /> <br /> <b>I can see Orders slowly conquering any land they are neighbor - but they need to have <i>whatever long contact</i> for that to work.</b> That's why Orders can be on Silk Road in the same time ( circa 2nd to 9th century ) - because Eastern Roman Empire have contacts with Turks, those with India ( that had already proto-Orders as Darshanas ) and China is just around corner. <b>HOWEVER protoNorse literally cut off their contacts with the old continent on migration, passing what would be described as Small Ice Age on the North.</b> So I do not see any Awakened contacts between Orders ( that did not converted Germans in 1st century AD ) and local Great Cults of Norse mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wise aren't Sleepers, nor bound by their cultural constraints. If Awakened Magellan decides to see what Mysteries are over the next horizon, they are going to get there. And keep in telepathic contact with whatever friends they've made while over there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T14:30:11-07:00","id":1220942,"title":"","content":"And, um, Wyrd. Please be aware that Scandinavia had and continued to have full contact with the rest of the continent and beyond from well before the Roman empire to long afterward. Not directly, in many cases, but passing through the &quot;Germanic&quot; peoples who were, themselves, descended from Scandinavians who moved south when the climate changed. <br /> <br /> They've dug out of [Swedish?] bogs &quot;Roman&quot; equipment with norse names and runes on it that were used in the 2nd century--and the winners tossed them into the bog as an offering. You had mercenaries flowing out of the north, goods flowing back, and the common people couldn't care less if that &quot;Germanic&quot; foederati spoke Frankish or Geatish. <br /> <br /> The Continent was much more unified in trade and flow of ideas than we have imagined in a progressive view of history, and the Dark Ages were dark only because folks weren't writing as much about them that got preserved. Not because they were huddled in shrinking globes of light. <br /> <br /> I'll let others argue how the mechanics of Mage work, except to say that I'm pretty sure things just get harder if you don't have sympathy and tools available--not impossible.<br /> <br /> Now, as to mages forming a group around Hel as a figure? We can assume that &quot;Hel&quot; the bale hound could be either a progenitor for the legends, or may have assumed the identity of Hel for her own purposes (e.g. scaring people stiff). Easy.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T14:35:51-07:00","id":1220947,"title":"","content":"I mean, we\u2019re talking about here the splat that did globalization before the word was even made up. One of the most prominent characteristics of Awakened society is that it is far less hindered by human barriers as we Sleepers know them, be it physical distance or cultural dissonance or gender identities or whatever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T14:40:19-07:00","id":1220952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1031595-dark-eras-the-fall-of-fenris?p=1220938#post1220938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wise aren't Sleepers, nor bound by their cultural constraints. If Awakened Magellan decides to see what Mysteries are over the next horizon, they are going to get there. And keep in telepathic contact with whatever friends they've made while over there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just wonder WHY would European Awakened move on to North. They have all they want Mysteries around them in Europe, especially with slow spread of Christianity and by this, Latin and Greek knowledge. Remember, past first migration of protoNorse in 1st century AD, North become locked in Small Ice Age. And then future Diamond German mages would - 'Should we go on to North? Nah, we have whole Teuroburg Forest to explore and up there there is only ice. What do you want to do with your life, Rikirun? Dig into ice - or understand questions of your homeland.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-21-2018, 05:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T14:45:00-07:00","id":1220954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1031595-dark-eras-the-fall-of-fenris?p=1220952#post1220952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I just wonder WHY would European Awakened move on to North. They have all they want Mysteries around them in Europe, especially with slow spread of Christianity and by this, Latin and Greek knowledge. Remember, past first migration of protoNorse in 1st century AD, North become locked in Small Ice Age. And then future Diamond German mages would - 'Should we go on to North? Nah, we have whole Teuroburg Forest to explore and up there there is only ice. What do you want to do with your life, Rikirun.'</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Why, Svabard the Wise, would you head south?&quot;<br /> &quot;Because it is warmer.&quot;<br /> [Meets Awakened down there, invites them to visit the hot spring up north some time]<br /> <br /> Or an Awakened is chasing some Mystery/Cryptid and ends up that way. Makes contact with local Wise for resources, shares ideas, agrees to keep in contact. Which spreads. Etc.<br /> <br /> You practically need a reason for there <i>not</i> to be contact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T14:52:09-07:00","id":1220958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1031595-dark-eras-the-fall-of-fenris?p=1220942#post1220942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And, um, Wyrd. Please be aware that Scandinavia had and continued to have full contact with the rest of the continent and beyond from well before the Roman empire to long afterward. Not directly, in many cases, but passing through the &quot;Germanic&quot; peoples who were, themselves, descended from Scandinavians who moved south when the climate changed.<br /> <br /> They've dug out of [Swedish?] bogs &quot;Roman&quot; equipment with norse names and runes on it that were used in the 2nd century--and the winners tossed them into the bog as an offering. You had mercenaries flowing out of the north, goods flowing back, and the common people couldn't care less if that &quot;Germanic&quot; foederati spoke Frankish or Geatish.<br /> <br /> The Continent was much more unified in trade and flow of ideas than we have imagined in a progressive view of history, and the Dark Ages were dark only because folks weren't writing as much about them that got preserved. Not because they were huddled in shrinking globes of light.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, but most of Norse population simply did not know what was on South, correct? Because I do not hear any sources stating that Normans were in, for example, Rome in 4th century AD. I do not even think their are sources pointing for them to be in nearest Teutoburg Forest of Germania even. I just do not think that there will be proper Order culture - NOT Darshana cults, they spring all around us as Mage canon - but proper structure of Diamond IF there will not one or two mage 'going over horizon'. Orders are something more than one or two lone walkers in the new terrain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T14:55:49-07:00","id":1220959,"title":"","content":"I tend to agree with Wyrd. Maybe not a great cult exactly, but definitely something like the Mutapa Empire, a 'convocation' that has it's own very distinct culture to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T15:18:31-07:00","id":1220968,"title":"","content":"Okay, I think we spammed a topic too much here - I moved <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1220967-dark-eras-how-orders-conquared-the-world\">discussion on Orders spreading the world</a> to the Mage forums, where it's place is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T15:26:53-07:00","id":1220970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1031595-dark-eras-the-fall-of-fenris?p=1220959#post1220959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tend to agree with Wyrd. Maybe not a great cult exactly, but definitely something like the Mutapa Empire, a 'convocation' that has it's own very distinct culture to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That I would be totally down with and it would be in line with how the Orders have spread around the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T15:30:45-07:00","id":1220972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1031595-dark-eras-the-fall-of-fenris?p=1220970#post1220970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That I would be totally down with and it would be in line with how the Orders have spread around the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>And no comes distinction on terminology on our points - I always meant Orders as 'particular hierarchical organisations <i>once</i> based on Darshana cults, with strong Greco-Roman terminology and symbolism'. You mean Orders=Darshanas. This is where it's misunderstanding. But let's just better talk about this on Mage forum topic on the matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T15:34:02-07:00","id":1220974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1031595-dark-eras-the-fall-of-fenris?p=1220959#post1220959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tend to agree with Wyrd. Maybe not a great cult exactly, but definitely something like the Mutapa Empire, a 'convocation' that has it's own very distinct culture to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, regional distinctions do exist, but we're still not talking about a place further than the universe here, not even <i>without magic</i>. The idea that there's no major Order presence is patently absurd in a time frame where the world is demonstrably connected, and there's not going to the usual culture wars between people who literally have the power call up nuclear energy hundreds of years before Sleepers get close to it and deal with entities beyond the comprehension of any culture that nevertheless represent a common connection for mages.<br /> <br /> Nordic-based Caucuses having their own flavor on things? Sure. Nordic Great Cults though? That time has gone and <i>passed</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 05-21-2018, 06:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T00:28:07-07:00","id":1221095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1031595-dark-eras-the-fall-of-fenris?p=1220974#post1220974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea that there's no major Order presence is patently absurd in a time frame where the world is demonstrably connected, and there's not going to the usual culture wars between people who literally have the power call up nuclear energy hundreds of years before Sleepers get close to it and deal with entities beyond the comprehension of any culture that nevertheless represent a common connection for mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, I know that was just an offhand example, but it does make me wonder. Could an Obrimos who has never conceived of radiation actually create or control it? I mean, I guess the &quot;symbols&quot; or radiation would exist, but would the local mages of the time be able to understand it enough to replicate and use it?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T00:42:02-07:00","id":1221097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gullinbursti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1031595-dark-eras-the-fall-of-fenris?p=1221095#post1221095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, I know that was just an offhand example, but it does make me wonder. Could an Obrimos who has never conceived of radiation actually create or control it? I mean, I guess the &quot;symbols&quot; or radiation would exist, but would the local mages of the time be able to understand it enough to replicate and use it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but it would probably take some serious exploration of <s>the Mother's Land</s> the Anima Mundi to really get it. Still, it's important to understand that an understanding of physics is not required for magic. Mages don't fly by manipulating the laws of physics to fly, they fly because, for them, the dream of humanity flying is stronger than the reality of it. A Master of Forces may not understand what nuclear radiation is, but they can certainly feel it out enough to strike people down with it.<br /> <br /> Mankind's dreams tend to always be <i>just</i> out of grasp, at some point or another.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 05-22-2018, 03:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T00:55:55-07:00","id":1221098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gullinbursti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1031595-dark-eras-the-fall-of-fenris?p=1221095#post1221095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, I know that was just an offhand example, but it does make me wonder. Could an Obrimos who has never conceived of radiation actually create or control it? I mean, I guess the &amp;quot;symbols&amp;quot; or radiation would exist, but would the local mages of the time be able to understand it enough to replicate and use it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I also say yes, and leave the radiation-mage puzzled why the hell this particular Forces Pattern he\u2019s controlling looks like a Death Pattern, being inundated with symbols of destructive transformation, and as an extension of that why the hell it screws up nearby Life Patterns so much in ways similar to but different from Patterns of poison and disease, despite being a pure Forces Pattern.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T03:20:44-07:00","id":1221111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1031595-dark-eras-the-fall-of-fenris?p=1221098#post1221098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I also say yes, and leave the radiation-mage puzzled why the hell this particular Forces Pattern he\u2019s controlling looks like a Death Pattern, being inundated with symbols of destructive transformation, and as an extension of that why the hell it screws up nearby Life Patterns so much in ways similar to but different from Patterns of poison and disease, despite being a pure Forces Pattern.</div> </div> </div> </div>Obsession time! Excellent description.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T06:29:08-07:00","id":1221139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1031595-dark-eras-the-fall-of-fenris?p=1220958#post1220958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, but most of Norse population simply did not know what was on South, correct? Because I do not hear any sources stating that Normans were in, for example, Rome in 4th century AD. I do not even think their are sources pointing for them to be in nearest Teutoburg Forest of Germania even. I just do not think that there will be proper Order culture - NOT Darshana cults, they spring all around us as Mage canon - but proper structure of Diamond IF there will not one or two mage 'going over horizon'. Orders are something more than one or two lone walkers in the new terrain.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most? That's a bit much to say. Some of course never left the farm, but they would hear the tales and it seems quite clear from the historical and archaelogical evidence that the Scandinavian Germanic peoples traveled widely and returned--often bearing the objects they traded for, plundered, or were given.<br /> <br /> Let's be clear as well: Norse were a people between 800 and 1300 AD--a specific group of Germanics who were one of the last to spread themselves in excited settling throughout Europe and parts of Asia. Earlier groups of Germanics were already present in these areas, often, and were either conquered or some assimilation took place. For example the Normans did not exist until a group of Norse negotiated land from the (originally Frankish, a Germanic tribe that invaded Gaul in the 5th century) king of France, and settled/defended the coast we now call Normandy.<br /> <br /> I'm not going to dig into JSTOR for scholarly articles. Here is a quick Google search: <a href=\"http://freya.theladyofthelabyrinth.com/?page_id=481\" target=\"_blank\">Scandinavia before the Viking Age \u2013 Migrations</a>. The point is that the people of this age were much more connected than we've been led to believe, and people moved around much more than the image of peasants and serfs (which were a later social innovations accompanying feudalism) implies. Now did they move around relatively less than during the height of Rome? Hard to say--but probably: Rome was a vast engine for enterprise and the movement of goods and riches, which draws adventurers and traders like iron to a lodestone. <br /> <br /> Looping back to the main topic, it seems clear to me that unless the influence of Ymir and the chaining of Fenrir (in the <i><b>uttermost </b></i>north, I presume) was very regional, it would have been noticed and could be investigated by Mages in particular, as well as other Uratha/Pure. What of that? At the very least, once the raids started you'd have folks asking &quot;why is this happening?&quot;<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T09:49:38-07:00","id":1221181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1031595-dark-eras-the-fall-of-fenris?p=1221139#post1221139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most? That's a bit much to say. Some of course never left the farm, but they would hear the tales and it seems quite clear from the historical and archaelogical evidence that the Scandinavian Germanic peoples traveled widely and returned--often bearing the objects they traded for, plundered, or were given.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, reading ( and quoting ) <a href=\"http://freya.theladyofthelabyrinth.com/?page_id=481\" target=\"_blank\">article</a> you linked I can see that some southern groups of Norse would make longer contact with Rome and related kingdoms even in 6th century. So true revolution of Viking Age was that they founded route to Europe <i><b>by sea</b></i>, not on long haul of walk on your feet from North.<br /> <br /> <i>'According to Jordanes (485-552) there was during the 6th century AD a federation of several Norwegian tribes under one leader, Rodulf (Hrolfr), and the tribal names mentioned are easily recognizable from (still existing) Norwegian regional names, people from the ancient tribal lands of Ranariki (\u201cRan\u00b4s Realm\u201d \u2013 \u00d8stfold in Norway and Bohusl\u00e4n in Sweden), Grenland, Agder, Telemark, Rogaland, Hordaland, H\u00e1leygjaland and Sami people (Granii, Augandzi, Eunixi, Taetel, Rugii, Aprochi). Apparently these warriors were \u201ctaller and wilder than the Germans\u201d and \u201cfought with beastly ferocity\u201d. Rodulf traveled all the way to Ravenna in Italy and was well received by the Gothic king Theoderic. Modern archaeologists are less and less surprised by such tales, since the southern and western coast of Norway had been in contact with southern European culture and aristocratic families for a long time already.</i> <i>The Scandinavians who ventured out also often returned. The death of Attila in 453 resulted in the freedom of several tribes who had been subject to the Huns for centuries already. The Rugii tribe, for example, had traveled all the way from Rogaland and south-west Norway (Avaldsnes high seat) and made a little realm for themselves in \u201cRugiland\u201d close to Vienna since the year 408 AD. Here they converted to Christianity, but to the heretic branch of Arianism. Together with the Herulii from Sk\u00e5ne in Sweden, most of them actually returned to their Scandinavian homelands after trouble with the Romans. The sources show that even after centuries abroad, the ties to the original homeland tribes were strong and thriving.'</i><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1031595-dark-eras-the-fall-of-fenris?p=1221139#post1221139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's be clear as well: Norse were a people between 800 and 1300 AD--a specific group of Germanics who were one of the last to spread themselves in excited settling throughout Europe and parts of Asia.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nitpicking, but Norse existed long before Viking Age in year 800 AD - they were in Scandinavia at least from last great Ice Age ( circa 12 000 BCE ). Rest of Germanic people are rooting directly from Norse forefathers that left Scandinavia from circa 800 BCE till 600 BCE, with good climate. So, in reality, Norse from 6th century AD were joining Europe to reclaim what they forefathers wanted to grasp in the first place.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Germanic_peoples#Origins\" target=\"_blank\">Wikipedia on Germanic people:</a><br /> <i>'Climatic change between 850 BCE to 760 BCE in Scandinavia and &quot;a later and more rapid one around 650 BCE might have triggered migrations to the coast of Eastern Germany and further toward the Vistula.<br /> The cultural phase of the late Bronze Age and early Iron Age in Europe (c. 1200\u2013600 BCE in temperate continental areas), known in contemporary terms as the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hallstatt_culture\" target=\"_blank\">Hallstatt culture</a> expanded from the south into this area and brought the early Germanic peoples under the influence of early Celtic (or pre Celtic) culture between 1200 BCE to 600 BCE, whereupon they began extracting <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bog_iron\" target=\"_blank\">bog iron</a> from the available ore in <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peat_bogs\" target=\"_blank\">peat bogs</a>.'</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-22-2018, 12:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T10:35:57-07:00","id":1221198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1031595-dark-eras-the-fall-of-fenris?p=1221181#post1221181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nitpicking, but Norse existed long before Viking Age in year 800 AD - they were in Scandinavia at least from last great Ice Age ( circa 12 000 BCE ). Rest of Germanic people are rooting directly from Norse forefathers that left Scandinavia from circa 800 BCE till 600 BCE, with good climate. So, in reality, Norse from 6th century AD were joining Europe to reclaim what they forefathers wanted to grasp in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Norse is just a grab-all for the tribes that lived in the North during the early middle ages.<br /> The actual tribes were Danes, Gutes, Geats, Swedes and Norwegians. And probably another bunch of smaller ones. The Frisians might be considered for this, and there is discussion whether or not the Jutes are a separate tribe, or they are either Danes or Gutes.<br /> <br /> The Norse themselves called themselves, collectively something that can be translated as &quot;Northmen&quot;, and a modern term is used all throughout the North even today; Nordbo. Which means &quot;North-living&quot;, that is, someone who lives in the North.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T10:45:44-07:00","id":1221205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1031595-dark-eras-the-fall-of-fenris?p=1221198#post1221198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Norse themselves called themselves, collectively something that can be translated as &quot;Northmen&quot;, and a modern term is used all throughout the North even today; Nordbo. Which means &quot;North-living&quot;, that is, someone who lives in the North.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great, I needed this name for my Viking game, had problem with Norse calling themselves in what future be modern Russia. And yes, before even by called 'Rus' by the local Sami people living there. 'Nordbo' it would be then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T10:59:37-07:00","id":1221210,"title":"","content":"Nordbo is the modern term used. As mentioned before, there are actually a multitude of groups that get variously referred to as Norse or Viking in the modern era.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-25T17:42:05-07:00","id":1222135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1031595-dark-eras-the-fall-of-fenris?p=1221205#post1221205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Great, I needed this name for my Viking game, had problem with Norse calling themselves in what future be modern Russia. And yes, before even by called 'Rus' by the local Sami people living there. 'Nordbo' it would be then.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with the word Rus, is that is a name for sailor. Same base as to row. The people of the eastern archipelago of Sweden used this to differentiate themselves from the people who lived inland, and took that term to apply to themselves.<br /> The reason that is Rus-Land, Russia, is because the Rus settled there.<br /> <br /> In Finnish, Sweden is called Ruotsi today, because it was the Rus who first came into contact with the Finnish tribes. Oh, and that archipelago is still today called Roslagen (compared with Danelagen, the Dane Law of England).<br /> <br /> Names are complicated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-26T01:52:47-07:00","id":1222187,"title":"","content":"I think for gameplay experience proto-Finnish people calling Vikings players as 'Rusi' would be enough - so calling future kingdom Rus (<i>Ru\u015b</i> in Polish ) will be natural. We do not run history course, it's just Werewolf RPG in historic setting. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T11:04:52-08:00","id":1290016,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1757_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1757\" data-vbnamecard=\"1757\">Acrozatarim</a> - Mr. Chris sir, are you perhaps intending to finish fleshing this out and release on the Storyteller's Vault or somesuch? I'm still quite interested in understanding what caused the Joten's hatred of Fenrir, back in the day (pre-Fall even) but don't want to steal thunder by picking at questions if you have a project in the works.<br /> <br /> Care to inform?<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T12:29:59-08:00","id":1290054,"title":"","content":"With the advent of the Storyteller's Vault, it's on my list of Things To Do, but obviously if you want to explore ideas for use in your games then I'm not going to stop you!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T10:34:31-08:00","id":1290424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1031595-dark-eras-the-fall-of-fenris?p=1290054#post1290054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With the advent of the Storyteller's Vault, it's on my list of Things To Do, but obviously if you want to explore ideas for use in your games then I'm not going to stop you!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, no... I mean you have more important things to do--such as drinking tea--rather than pop down my chimney shouting &quot;'Allo 'allo here, that's not how Fenris Falls! And that NPC--total bollock! Bad cricket all around! No GM biscuit for you, sir!&quot;<br /> <br /> Ehem. That said, I sketch-plot out far in advance (years), and if I know something is eventually coming--as you've indicated may, it helps. So thanks!<br /> <br /> [Current plot points include back-and-forth setting jumps from the 6200BC <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Storegga_Slide\" target=\"_blank\">Storegga Slide</a> and concurrent drowning of the Doggerland (with, ehem, shining Valusia), to the creation of Hela, to the viking raids. Just don't know how it ties together, yet.]<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}